<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John II Komnenos</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1087">1087</a>–1143</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as John II Comnenus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John II Komnenos was Byzantine emperor from 1118 to 1143, the son of Alexios I. He fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pechenegs">Pechenegs</a>, Hungarians and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbs">Serbs</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkans">Balkans</a> and recovered lands from the Turks in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>. In 1137 to 1138 he campaigned in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cilicia">Cilicia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>, forcing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch">Antioch</a> to accept his overlordship and besieging Shaizar with Frankish allies. Admired for his justice and piety, he died after a hunting accident.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-ii-komnenos.jpg" alt="John II Komnenos" width="320" height="510" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jean_II_Comnene.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
